  "definicoes": {
    "pi_frac_sentinela": "y[:,0] >= 299.0 (PL_TARGET_MAX_VALID); e3_inferencia_por_populacao.py:175,951; alvo_stats.py:'sentinela'",
    "r2_teto": "corr_pearson(RSSI[~sentinela], -log10(max(dist_nearest_m,1.0)))**2, over the indicated POPULATION (whole cell or test set); COPY of the corr() function of EVIDENCIA_RESUBMISSAO/scripts/alvo_stats.py:24-27, reused by e3_alvos_dataset_v2_multi.py (generator of the alvo_stats_*_v2.json files). dist_nearest_m is the field of the tensor itself (rf_data['terrain'].dist_nearest_m), the same one used by alvo_stats.py and by e3_inferencia_por_populacao.py.",
    "mae_constante": "mean(|RSSI - median(RSSI)|) over the SAME population (whole cell or test set); COPY of EVIDENCIA_RESUBMISSAO/scripts/fismat_controle_negativo_alvo.py:31-35 (field 'MAE_preditor_constante_mediana'). The constant is the median of the column, NOT the sentinel value by definition -- in the 16 cells it collapses to -110.0 dBm (== floor/sentinel) because frac_sentinela>0.5 in every cell and every partition; hence mae_constante_teste == mae_constante_piso_teste == mae_constante_treino_aplicada_teste in all 16 cells (see por_celula).",
    "split": "Literal COPY of train_gnn_c0_spatial.py:351-373 (latlon_graus_para_metros) and :412-487 (split_espacial_3vias) + SpatialKFold from GNN_RF_V2/03_training/spatial_cv.py, via e3_inferencia_por_populacao.py. grid_km/buffer_km/split_frac/split_seed read from run_rec['config']; idx_sha256_global of the 3 partitions checked against run_c0c1cf_<cidade>_s42_<Q>_g10b2.json (16/16 OK)."
  },
